Comment: glycin is offered under either licence (upstream's LICENSE reads
 "MPL-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later"). Corresponding source for this build: the release
 tarball https://download.gnome.org/sources/glycin/2.2/glycin-2.2.1.tar.xz plus the patches
 in patches/ of the amber-glycin source package. The libraries are shipped as separate,
 dynamically linked .so files under the private path /usr/lib/amber-glycin/, so the LGPL's
 shared-library terms apply. The libraries and loaders statically link Rust crates from
 crates.io, pinned by the tarball's Cargo.lock; each crate keeps its own licence (chiefly
 MIT or Apache-2.0, with some BSD, Zlib and Unlicense, and the glycin crates themselves
 under MPL-2.0 or LGPL-2.1+), recorded in that crate's own metadata.

